<comment datatype="string">&lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=5-METHYLTHIOADENOSINE"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5'-thioadenosine&lt;/a&gt; (MTA) metabolism in a &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1085"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Rhodospirillum rubrum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; mutant with a disrupted &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-15512"&gt;mtnA&lt;/a&gt; gene stopped at the level of &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-1063"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5-thio-D-ribulose 1-phosphate&lt;/a&gt;, supporting its proposed role as &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=MONOMER-17870"&gt;methylthioribose-1-phosphate isomerase&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23042035"&gt;Erb12&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
The &lt;a href="/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-15512"&gt;mtnA&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1085"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Rhodospirillum rubrum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has been cloned as a His&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt; construct and expressed in &lt;a href="/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-562"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and the recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity and tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; [&lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23042035"&gt;Erb12&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/31950558"&gt;North20&lt;/a&gt;]. It was shown to be active with both &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-15199"&gt;5-deoxy-&amp;alpha;-D-ribose 1-phosphate&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=CPD-444"&gt;&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-methyl-5-thio-&amp;alpha;-D-ribose 1-phosphate&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/31950558"&gt;North20&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
